      },
      "text": "Exploration is the systematic extension of known geography. It is driven by commercial incentives (trade routes, resources), political goals (sovereignty, strategy), scientific curiosity (natural history, cartography), and individual ambition — often in combination. The history of exploration is also the history of contact, conquest, displacement, and death — the ethical weight is inseparable from the achievement."
